## Details

Reads a Kairos VM's `<short_name>-stow status --json --values` over SSH, as the SSH user, without
managing it. Nothing on the VM changes. The read is bounded by 5 minutes. Another project's
install (`Another project's install`) is an error.

| Argument | | |
|---|---|---|
| `name`, `short_name` | required | The project's name (compared with the status's) and the installer's short name, one path element each. |
| `host` | required | The VM's address, reached by the system `ssh`. |
| `port`, `user`, `private_key_file`, `known_hosts_line` | optional | As `stowage_vm_install`'s; `user` and `known_hosts_line` (the VM's own key) required with `host`. |

| Attribute | |
|---|---|
| `id` | `<host>/<short_name>-stow`. |
| `installed`, `previous` | `{version, revision, installer}` (`installer` null on a VM); null before the first install, and when the install keeps no release for `rollback`. |
| `channel`, `status` | As the resource's. |
| `inputs` | The input keys the install records, sorted, never a value; null when the installer does not tell. |
| `registry`, `registry_ca_digest`, `address` | What the first install recorded; null when the status gives none. |
| `pull_login` | Whether the install holds its own registry login (`status --json --values` `pull_login`); null from an installer that does not tell (before Stowage 0.40.0). |
